//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="577\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: type.int.shift
//!
//! wolf-lang#755 (s237): a function with no `if`, loop, call or index
//! is lowered as one block, and its locals are kept for that block
//! alone. A construct that branches in the middle of an expression ends
//! the block, so a local declared before it and read after it had no
//! definition: a plain `<<` by a constant count of a value that is not
//! one (the round trip's check). Native and release panicked at s237's
//! head `822120f0`, the shift's own branches being new there; trunk had
//! no branch to split on, "use of a variable with no definition on some
//! path". The checked machine and lupin 0.1.52 printed what this row
//! says.

fn f(x: u64) -> u64 {
    let y = x + 1
    let z = x << 3
    y + z
}

fn main() {
    print("{f(64)}")
}
